       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some references list 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Typical single dose:** 500\u20131000 mg, and no more than 1000 mg per administration.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want. If you do intend 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I can enter it with a note. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
