     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also about twice the maximum, and the risk is serious: lactic acidosis. Metformin's glucose-lowering effect plateaus at about 2,000 mg/day, so a higher dose adds risk with little benefit. Failure on standard dosing is usually handled by adding or switching agents, not by exceeding the metformin maximum.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or whatever dose you choose within the limit.\n- **Pursue the above-maximum dose through pharmacy.** Your pharmacist and the specialist can document the rationale and approve an override. Once that's done, the order can go through the system's high-dose override process.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter a dose within the range, and which one."
      }
     ],
